<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="Swing48-Gm-Theme" spTempo="258">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1948
Composer:	Django Reinhardt
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	12-bar blues
Style:	Gypsy Swing / Manouche Jazz
Key:	G minor

Swing 48 is an original composition by Django Reinhardt,
written and first recorded in 1948 during the final phase of
his career. The tune represents his continuing musical
evolution, blending the traditional spirit of Gypsy Swing
with the more modern harmonic ideas that increasingly
fascinated him after World War II. Created as part of
Django&apos;s late creative period—when he became more
interested in bebop and contemporary American
jazz—​Swing 48 remains one of the finest examples of his
later compositional style, balancing timeless swing
character with modern harmonic colors.</spComments>
